# Backend: Security + Production Readiness

## Auth + cookies
- Keep JWTs in `HttpOnly` cookies.
- Set `secure: true` only when behind HTTPS.
- Prefer `sameSite: "Lax"` for typical web apps unless you have strict requirements.

## Input hardening
- Validate and normalize all user input.
- Sanitize any file uploads (limits + MIME checking).

## Sensitive data
- Never log or return secrets.
- Prefer storing external IDs (`public_id`) in URLs instead of internal numeric IDs.

## Defensive middleware (recommended additions)
- Add `helmet` for common HTTP security headers.
- Add rate limiting (e.g., login/refresh endpoints) to reduce brute force risk.
- Consider CSRF protection if relying on cookies for auth.

## DB safety
- Avoid `sequelize.sync({ alter: true })` in production.
- Use migrations + seed scripts in CI/CD.
